            <ArticleTitle>[The developing risks of the allergic child].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>363-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>6% of infants are allergic to egg. 50% of them are at risk of becoming sensitive to pneumoallergens and of whom 50% develop asthma. These evolutionary risks which are the allergy &quot;course&quot; of the child may be avoided by a precise interrogation which is orientated towards detection by in vitro tests of F x 5 for foods and Phadiatop for pneumoallergens. The responsible allergens may themselves be shown by skin tests, measurement of specific IgE by CAP-RAST made by UNICAP.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
